.TH geectl-remote-list-files 1  "geectl-remote-list-files 0.2.2" 
.SH NAME
geectl\-remote\-list\-files \- List the files of a package
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgeectl remote list\-files\fR [\fB\-\-rev\fR] [\fB\-\-include\-deleted\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIPROJECT\fR> <\fIPACKAGE\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
List the files of a package
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-rev\fR \fI<REV>\fR
List the files as of this revision (default: latest): a revision number or a srcmd5
.TP
\fB\-\-include\-deleted\fR
Include files from deleted revisions in the listing: the files of a deleted package, for asking whether a project ever held it. Requires OBS credentials: the deleted listing reads the authenticated source route
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIPROJECT\fR>
The project the package lives in
.TP
<\fIPACKAGE\fR>
The package to list
.SH VERSION
v0.2.2
